          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Where in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+geometry"} algebraic geometry
            one considers
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spaces"} spaces
            which are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Isbell+duality"} formally dual
            to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+rings"} commutative rings
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-rigs"} 2-rigs
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+categories"} tensor categories
            or more generally to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} tensor (∞,1)-categories
          %p
            Curiously, the more general idea of regarding certain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+categories"} abelian categories
            and certain linear
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A-%E2%88%9E+categories"} A-∞ categories
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"}> stable (∞,1)-categories
            ) as analogs of categories of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasicoherent+sheaves"} quasicoherent sheaves
            on some space (i.e. ignoring the monoidal structure) is much older, this is the program of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+noncommutative+geometry"} derived noncommutative geometry
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "derived+algebraic+geometry#RelationToDerivedNoncommutativeGeometry"} derived algebraic geometry – Relation to noncommutative geometry
          %p
            The systematic use of the tensor product structure here goes back to (
            %a{:href => "#Balmer02"}> Balmer 02
            ) and the concept of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum+of+a+tensor+triangulated+category"} spectrum of a tensor triangulated category
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Lurie"} Lurie
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+scheme"} affine scheme
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#CJF11"} CJF 11
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum+of+a+tensor+triangulated+category"} spectrum of a tensor triangulated category
            %li
